Binary OPENSTEP nib support
===========================

GSOpenStepTypedStream.m is an Objective-C 1.0 compatible typed stream reader
written for GNUstep GUI.  It keeps its parsed graph in private C structures
declared in GSOpenStepTypedStream.h.  No NIBMAKER parser source is included.
The historical class layouts used by GSOpenStepNibReader.m were researched
with NIBMAKER-FOR-OPENSTEP's format documentation and examples (commit
bcc7c1a09e0be874f1df259e809517a89b765986).  Thank you to u/These_Magician_3789 on Reddit for his work on the original idea.

The reader accepts streamer versions 3 and 4, both typedstream byte orders,
and checks bounds, references, nesting, array counts, and total allocations.
GSOpenStepNibReader.m converts supported historical objects to an in-memory
binary keyed archive for the existing GSNibLoader path.  Unknown classes and
unsupported layouts fail before application objects are instantiated.

The supported class versions and explicit semantic limitations are encoded
in GSOpenStepNibReader.m.  Tests/gui/NSNibLoading/README.openstep describes
the regression tests and fixture generation.
